From c782767a55df3db7bd8a7ed7b4f551935ad651b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:10:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] [TSReader] Change the PTS diff with the first frame of
 the new segment

The reader took the diff of a new segment when the demuxer parsed the
first PES header of that segment. The video parser emits a frame only
after the start of the next frame, so the last two video frames of the
previous segment came after that header and took the diff of the new
segment.

The demuxer now marks the first PES of each stream after the segment
change in the elementary stream buffer. A packet that starts at the
mark or later is from the new segment, the same rule the parsers use to
assign a PTS to a frame. The reader takes the new diff with the first
packet of the new segment after the video has no frames of the previous
segment left. A muxed reader has one diff for both streams, and the
session applies the diff of the timing stream to all samples, so the
diff follows the video. A cleared buffer keeps the mark at the buffer
start, so after a seek or at the stream start the diff applies at once.

The TS, WebM and ADTS tests give each segment a different diff, so the
tests check where the diff changes, also for video only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
